{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "א' דויקרא", :translit "alef d'vayikra", :gloss "the alef of vayikra"} {:he "ויקר", :translit "vayikar", :gloss "and He happened [upon]"} {:he "ויקרא אל משה", :translit "vayikra el mosheh", :gloss "and He called to Moses"} {:he "אמ\"ו בעטרה שעטרה לו אמו", :translit "amu ba'atarah she'atarah lo imo", :gloss "his mother — with a crown that his mother crowned him"} {:he "ואש תהיה לילה בו", :translit "v'esh tihyeh laylah bo", :gloss "and fire shall be kept burning in it"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :rashei-tevot, :phrase "ויקרא אל משה", :spells "אמו"} {:kind :other, :note "Small alef of ויקרא: Moses wished to write ויקר (chance appearance, as with Balaam) but God told him to include the alef; he wrote it small."} {:kind :other, :note "Moses reversed the normal word order, placing וידבר before God's name, as one who courteously addresses a friend directly."} {:kind :other, :note "Adjacency: ואש תהיה לילה בו is followed by ויקרא אל משה — since God called and spoke with him, Moses's face burned like fire."}], :frame {:text "The contrast between ויקרא (with alef, deliberate calling) and ויקר (without alef, chance encounter) is drawn from Numbers 23:4, where God \"happened upon\" Balaam (ויקר אלהים אל בלעם). The Tanchuma (Vayikra 5) and Vayikra Rabbah 1:15 develop the tradition that the small alef reflects Moses's humility — he did not want to presume God intentionally called him. The midrashic idea that Moses's face radiated light from God's speech to him is attested in Exodus 34:29–30 (קרן עור פניו).", :sources ["Numbers 23:4" "Tanchuma Vayikra 5" "Vayikra Rabbah 1:15" "Exodus 34:29–30"]}} {:quotes [{:he "בכל מסעיהם ויקרא אל משה", :translit "b'chol mas'ehem vayikra el mosheh", :gloss "in all their journeys and He called to Moses"} {:he "ע\"פ ה' יסעו", :translit "al pi Hashem yisa'u", :gloss "at the mouth of Hashem they would journey"} {:he "אנכי ה' אלהיך", :translit "anochi Hashem Elokekha", :gloss "I am Hashem your God"} {:he "זאת התורה לעולה", :translit "zot haTorah la'olah", :gloss "this is the Torah for the burnt offering"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 5, :occurrences []} {:kind :masorah, :count 9, :occurrences []} {:kind :other, :note "Five alefs in the verse correspond to the five books of the Torah."} {:kind :other, :note "Nine words in the verse parallel nine words in אנכי ה' אלהיך and in זאת התורה לעולה, linking Torah study to the sacrificial order."}], :frame {:text "The equation of Torah study with sacrifice is explicitly taught in Menachot 110a, which states that one who engages in Torah study is regarded as if he offered all the sacrifices, citing verses such as זאת התורה לעולה. The phrase על פי ה' יסעו, describing Israel's journeys at God's direction, appears in Numbers 9:20, and Numbers 9:23 summarizes all their travels as על פי ה' by the word בכל מסעיהם.", :sources ["Menachot 110a" "Numbers 9:20" "Numbers 9:23"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :rashei-tevot, :phrase "ויקרא אל משה", :spells "אמו", :letters ["ו" "א" "מ"], :by :selah, :order :bag} {:kind :other, :note "Small alef of ויקרא: Moses wished to write ויקר (chance appearance, as with Balaam) but God told him to include the alef; he wrote it small.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Moses reversed the normal word order, placing וידבר before God's name, as one who courteously addresses a friend directly.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Adjacency: ואש תהיה לילה בו is followed by ויקרא אל משה — since God called and spoke with him, Moses's face burned like fire.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :masorah, :count 5, :occurrences [], :by :selah, :located []} {:kind :masorah, :count 9, :occurrences [], :by :selah, :located []} {:kind :other, :note "Five alefs in the verse correspond to the five books of the Torah.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Nine words in the verse parallel nine words in אנכי ה' אלהיך and in זאת התורה לעולה, linking Torah study to the sacrificial order.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:21:59.308929069Z", :model "glm-5.2"}